---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Sumi Support — Help With Your Scientific Calculator"
  description="Find help with Sumi’s exact answers, calculation history, themes and settings, or contact the developer with a question or bug report."
>
  <section class="page-heading wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">HERE TO HELP</p>
    <h1>
      A little
      <br />
      <span>clarity.</span>
    </h1>
    <p class="page-intro">
      Questions, bug reports and suggestions are welcome.
      <br />
      <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email} ↗</a>
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="support-content wrap">
    <div class="support-intro">
      <h2>
        Make yourself
        <br />
        at home.
      </h2>
      <p>
        New to Sumi? Start with our practical guides to fractions, exact answers
        and equation solving.
      </p>
      <a href="/guides/" class="text-link">
        Open the notebook <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
      </a>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-list">
      <details open>
        <summary>
          Why does Sumi show a fraction or square root?
          <span aria-hidden="true">+</span>
        </summary>
        <p>
          Sumi keeps supported answers exact. Press <strong>S⇔D</strong> to
          switch between the exact form and its decimal value.{' '}
          <a href="/guides/exact-answers/">Learn about exact answers.</a>
        </p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>
          How do I see previous calculations?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span>
        </summary>
        <p>
          Tap the history key (the clock icon) or drag up from the keypad.
          Tapping an entry brings its expression back for editing.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>
          How do I change the theme?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span>
        </summary>
        <p>
          Open Settings with the sliders icon and choose <strong>Paper</strong>,{' '}
          <strong>Ink</strong> or <strong>System</strong> under Theme.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>
          How do I change angle units or decimal places?
          <span aria-hidden="true">+</span>
        </summary>
        <p>
          Open Settings and choose <strong>Angle unit</strong> for degrees,
          radians or gradians. Under <strong>Number format</strong>, choose Fix,
          Sci, Norm1 or Norm2. Fix lets you set Decimal places; tap S⇔D if you
          are viewing an exact result.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>
          How do I copy a result?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span>
        </summary>
        <p>Long-press the result to copy it to the clipboard.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>
          How do I delete my data?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span>
        </summary>
        <p>
          Everything Sumi stores lives on your device.{' '}
          <strong>Reset all</strong> in Settings clears memory, settings and
          history. Deleting the app removes its stored data. See the{' '}
          <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>
          What is the tip jar?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span>
        </summary>
        <p>
          Sumi is free with no ads. The tip jar in Settings lets you leave a
          small one-off tip through the platform’s store. Tips unlock nothing
          and are never required.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>
          What should I include in a bug report?
          <span aria-hidden="true">+</span>
        </summary>
        <p>
          Email the calculation and the keys you pressed, the result you
          expected, and your app version and device model. Include a screenshot
          if it helps show the issue.
        </p>
      </details>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
